  "final_answer": "For the 10 K Cu foil, I normalized μ(E), removed the AUTOBK background, and fit the Cu–Cu first shell over **k = 3–10 Å⁻¹** and **R = 1–3 Å**. The fit varied \\(S_0^2\\), \\(\\Delta E_0\\), \\(\\sigma^2\\), and \\(\\Delta R\\), then repeated the fit across five nearby k/R windows; it was judged **robust**.\n\n- **Nearest-neighbour Cu–Cu distance:** **2.552 Å**\n- **Practical reportable value:** **2.55 Å**\n- **Formal fit uncertainty:** about **±0.001 Å**\n- **Window-sensitivity spread:** about **0.003 Å** overall\n\nSo you can trust the result comfortably to **a few hundredths of an ångström**—reporting **2.55 Å** is justified. I would not claim precision much better than roughly **±0.01 Å** without independently addressing absolute energy calibration and model/systematic errors."
